{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.he4_conditioning_regime_differs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.he4_conditioning_regime_differs","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotCancellationConditioning.lean#L157-L165","doc":"**The ⁴He cancellation is two orders of magnitude sharper than the mirror pair's.**  `κ(T)` and\n`κ(³He)` exceed `κ(⁴He)` by more than `25×`, so the four isotopes do not share a conditioning regime:\nany statement that reads the cross-isotope `C_knot` spread as a uniform measurement of per-knot\nvariation is comparing one ill-conditioned point against three well-conditioned ones. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.mirror_pair_well_conditioned","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.mirror_pair_well_conditioned","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotCancellationConditioning.lean#L145-L155","doc":"**The mirror pair is well conditioned** — `κ(T) > 1/4` and `κ(³He) > 1/4`.\n\nThis is the defensive half of the conditioning analysis.  `CKnotNonUniversal.no_level_only_closure`\nexcludes the level-only rescale class using the `(B, S)` pairs of the triton and helion; both sit at\n`κ` above a quarter, i.e. within a factor `4` of a perfectly conditioned sum.  So that scope-(b)\nexclusion is **not** touched by anything proved here — the ill-conditioning is localised on `⁴He`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.he4_cancellation_below_one_percent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.he4_cancellation_below_one_percent","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotCancellationConditioning.lean#L136-L143","doc":"**`⁴He` sits on a sub-percent cancellation:** `κ(⁴He) = |S| / Σ|t_λ| < 1/100`.\n\nBy `exists_annihilating_perturbation`, a per-block relative correction of sup-norm under `1%` sends\n`S(⁴He)` to zero and `C_knot(⁴He)` to `+∞`.  The reported `C_knot(⁴He) = 290.007` — which is what\nproduces the headline cross-isotope spread `59.12×` — is therefore an amplified cancellation, not a\nmeasurement of `290×` of missing physics. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.T_He3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.T_He3","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotCancellationConditioning.lean#L133-L134","doc":"`T(³He) = Σ_λ |t_λ|` for the helion at `H₉`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.absS_He3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.absS_He3","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotCancellationConditioning.lean#L130-L131","doc":"`|S(³He)|` — magnitude of the master binding sum for the helion at `H₉`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.T_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.T_T","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotCancellationConditioning.lean#L127-L128","doc":"`T(T) = Σ_λ |t_λ|` for the triton at `H₉`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.absS_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.absS_T","kind":"def","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotCancellationConditioning.lean#L124-L125","doc":"`|S(T)|` — magnitude of the master binding sum for the triton at `H₉`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.T_He4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.T_He4","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotCancellationConditioning.lean#L121-L122","doc":"`T(⁴He) = Σ_λ |t_λ|` — the absolute-term total at `H₁₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.absS_He4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.absS_He4","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotCancellationConditioning.lean#L118-L119","doc":"`|S(⁴He)|` — magnitude of the master binding sum at `H₁₂` (77 partitions). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.exists_annihilating_perturbation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.exists_annihilating_perturbation","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotCancellationConditioning.lean#L82-L109","doc":"**The conditioning bound is sharp: a perturbation of sup-norm exactly `κ` annihilates the sum.**\n\nTake `δ i = -(S / T) · sign(t i)` with `S = Σ t i`, `T = Σ|t i|`.  Then `t i · δ i = -(S/T)·|t i|`, so\nthe perturbed total is `S - (S/T)·T = 0`, while `‖δ‖_∞ = |S|/T = κ`.\n\nConsequence for the deficit ratio: when `κ` is small, `C_knot = B/(m_e·|S|)` is not merely\nimprecise — a per-block relative correction of size `κ` sends `|S|` to `0` and `C_knot` to `+∞`, and\ncorrections slightly larger flip the sign of `S`.  So `C_knot(⁴He) = 290.007`, sitting at\n`κ < 1/100`, carries essentially no information about the size of the missing per-block structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.perturbed_sum_dist_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CKnotCancellationConditioning.perturbed_sum_dist_le","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CKnotCancellationConditioning.lean#L62-L80","doc":"**Conditioning bound for a relative per-block perturbation.**  If every block term `t i` is\nperturbed multiplicatively, `t i ↦ t i · (1 + δ i)`, with sup-norm `‖δ‖_∞ ≤ ε`, then the total moves\nby at most `ε · Σ|t i|`.\n\nDividing by `|Σ t i|` and writing `κ = |Σ t i| / Σ|t i|`, the *relative* move of the total is bounded\nby `ε / κ`.  That is the precise sense in which `1/κ` is the condition number of the master binding\nmagnitude: for `⁴He`, `κ ≈ 0.008`, so a sub-percent per-block correction is amplified into an\norder-one change in `|S|` and hence in `C_knot`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}